WEBVTT

00:00:02.710 --> 00:00:04.080
<i>That day, that time...</i>

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:08.920
<i>A one-kilometer-radius area of Shibuya,</i>
<i>the place where we were,</i>

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:12.550
<i>was cut out</i>
<i>and transported to the future.</i>

00:00:13.760 --> 00:00:16.470
<i>It was the year 2388.</i>

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:20.220
<i>Outside of Shibuya</i>
<i>was a vast mysterious wasteland.</i>

00:00:21.680 --> 00:00:25.560
<i>Then my close friends</i>
<i>since elementary school and I</i>

00:00:25.940 --> 00:00:28.150
<i>were given the task</i>
<i>of protecting the people.</i>

00:00:29.190 --> 00:00:31.820
<i>That's because we are</i>
<i>the only ones who can use</i>

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:35.490
<i>the Combat Suits built with</i>
<i>future technology, called String Puppets.</i>

00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:38.080
<i>Milo's words to me that day,</i>

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:41.080
<i>my destiny to protect everyone,</i>

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.960
<i>is about to become reality</i>
<i>in this future world.</i>

00:00:46.290 --> 00:00:49.000
<i>The protesters are gathering</i>
<i>on Aoyama Street.</i>

00:00:49.090 --> 00:00:50.710
<i>Their leader is probably a student.</i>

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.710
<i>Their numbers are unclear</i>
<i>at the moment. Over.</i>

00:00:52.800 --> 00:00:54.680
What's going to happen to us?

00:00:55.010 --> 00:00:57.300
We're supposed to protect Shibuya now?

00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.850
It depends on whether we can
actually use the machine Daisuke is using.

00:01:04.480 --> 00:01:06.440
Are we really going to use that thing?

00:01:06.520 --> 00:01:08.690
Oh, will it be like a part-time job?

00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.440
What? I'm not sure.

00:01:12.730 --> 00:01:14.110
<i>How are the children?</i>

00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:16.360
They seem calmer than last night.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:18.620
But should we really ask high schoolers
for help?

00:01:18.700 --> 00:01:22.160
As long as we don't have any grasp
on the situation,

00:01:22.240 --> 00:01:24.620
we will have to
rely on Milo's information.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:26.830
-Assist them.
-<i>Yes, sir.</i>

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.130
And keep tabs on Milo.

00:01:29.210 --> 00:01:31.460
<i>Include every detail in your report.</i>

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.590
<i>-Is that understood?</i>
-Understood.

00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:37.470
No enemies detected
at the destination point.

00:01:37.550 --> 00:01:39.090
We should head there now.

00:01:39.930 --> 00:01:41.470
Everyone, we're moving out!

00:01:41.560 --> 00:01:42.720
-Okay!
-Okay!

00:01:43.270 --> 00:01:44.730
Daisuke, we're going.

00:01:44.810 --> 00:01:46.060
All right!

00:01:46.140 --> 00:01:47.520
Hold on!

00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:49.440
Mom?

00:01:49.520 --> 00:01:52.820
Take this. It's lunch.
There's enough for everyone.

00:01:53.150 --> 00:01:55.940
I'm volunteering
at the emergency food distribution.

00:01:56.030 --> 00:01:57.490
-This is the least--
-Okay, got it!

00:01:58.070 --> 00:01:59.450
Bye. Be careful.

00:02:00.070 --> 00:02:02.240
-Be careful!
-Your mom is sweet.

00:02:02.370 --> 00:02:03.740
She's just annoying.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:07.080
Hey, let's get going
and take care of this quickly.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:10.540
Now, as the Shibuya Defense Service

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:15.130
or SDS, we will retrieve the two remaining
Anti-Revisions Wearable Combat System,

00:02:15.210 --> 00:02:17.170
String Puppets.

00:02:17.720 --> 00:02:18.680
-Roger.
-Okay.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:21.850
"Service"?

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.500
Is this really the future?

00:04:11.580 --> 00:04:13.710
It feels like an anime,
or movie, or something.

00:04:13.790 --> 00:04:17.290
It doesn't feel real.
I guess we just have to accept it.

00:04:17.710 --> 00:04:19.880
Yes, this is our reality now.

00:04:19.960 --> 00:04:23.300
Milo, what happened to the world?

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:25.890
<i>I've already told the Mayor and others.</i>

00:04:25.970 --> 00:04:29.010
<i>That information doesn't come so far</i>
<i>down the chain to someone like me.</i>

00:04:29.100 --> 00:04:30.220
It was a pandemic.

00:04:30.600 --> 00:04:31.600
<i>A pandemic?</i>

00:04:32.310 --> 00:04:33.850
About 350 years ago,

00:04:34.270 --> 00:04:37.150
the world was overwhelmed by the spread
of a mysterious pathogen.

00:04:37.230 --> 00:04:39.230
Like pests? Or cholera?

00:04:39.820 --> 00:04:44.570
<i>No.</i><i>A disease so terrible that</i>
<i>the nations of the world fell to pieces.</i>

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:47.740
What? You mean the entire world perished?

00:04:47.820 --> 00:04:51.120
Wait! Is it an airborne disease?

00:04:52.370 --> 00:04:53.370
Don't worry.

00:04:53.710 --> 00:04:55.670
The pandemic itself has died off.

00:04:56.000 --> 00:04:58.250
We've verified the pathogen's death.

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.500
It's fine here.

00:05:00.710 --> 00:05:03.800
From here on, I'll take the lead to scout.

00:05:03.920 --> 00:05:06.090
You all head to the destination
I showed you earlier

00:05:06.180 --> 00:05:07.590
and retrieve the two String Puppets.

00:05:07.680 --> 00:05:11.310
Daisuke, provide cover for everyone.
I'll send the location later.

00:05:11.810 --> 00:05:14.100
Got it. I'll protect everyone!

00:05:18.100 --> 00:05:22.150
<i>So, what do you think about</i>
<i>what the woman of the future told us?</i>

00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:25.320
<i>Let's keep silent</i>
<i>about the world perishing from a pandemic.</i>

00:05:25.450 --> 00:05:26.450
<i>It would cause a riot.</i>

00:05:26.530 --> 00:05:27.780
You're right.

00:05:28.110 --> 00:05:31.370
There is already unrest
amongst the residents here.

00:05:31.950 --> 00:05:34.540
What's the update
on the temporary shelters?

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:37.620
We're having the students stay
at their schools.

00:05:38.040 --> 00:05:43.460
We have the adults in hotels,
but there's no community infrastructure.

00:05:44.460 --> 00:05:46.760
This is bad, really bad.

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:51.430
More importantly, why did the Revisions
transport Shibuya to this time?

00:05:51.680 --> 00:05:54.850
Apparently, we've been abducted here
to be used for some experiment.

00:05:55.270 --> 00:05:58.900
This obvious threat would cause a panic,
and the community would collapse.

00:05:59.310 --> 00:06:00.560
When will the retrieval

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:02.690
of the Anti-Revisions
Wearable Combat System finish?

00:06:02.770 --> 00:06:04.860
They're scheduled
to come back this afternoon.

00:06:08.070 --> 00:06:09.610
Let's see.

00:06:09.910 --> 00:06:11.780
<i>Displaying updated data.</i>

00:06:13.990 --> 00:06:15.290
What? All the way out there?

00:06:15.370 --> 00:06:16.710
<i>-What's wrong?</i>
-Well...

00:06:16.870 --> 00:06:19.460
Well, isn't that too far from everyone?

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:24.630
<i>Your job is to shoot at the targets</i>
<i>I indicate if the enemy appears.</i>

00:06:24.710 --> 00:06:27.420
<i>Then I won't be able to protect</i>
<i>everyone directly. I--</i>

00:06:27.510 --> 00:06:29.590
<i>I'll figure out how to protect everyone.</i>

00:06:29.680 --> 00:06:31.800
<i>What? But I'm the one who should do that.</i>

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:35.310
<i>You're the one who told me</i>
<i>to never forget that it was my destiny!</i>

00:06:35.390 --> 00:06:37.270
Sorry, but I know nothing of that.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:39.020
But you...

00:06:40.230 --> 00:06:41.230
Are you...

00:06:42.770 --> 00:06:43.980
<i>really Milo?</i>

00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.360
<i>I am Milo.</i>

00:06:45.530 --> 00:06:47.030
<i>I have no other name.</i>

00:06:47.110 --> 00:06:50.360
<i>The Milo I know was the one</i>
<i>who gave a prophecy about my future.</i>

00:06:50.450 --> 00:06:52.070
What's the matter, Daisuke?

00:06:52.160 --> 00:06:55.490
-He's a bit traumatized.
-It's a sensitive topic.

00:06:55.580 --> 00:06:57.160
<i>Daisuke, follow orders.</i>

00:06:57.620 --> 00:07:01.290
-I should stay close to protect them.
<i>-Daisuke, give it a rest.</i>

00:07:01.370 --> 00:07:02.750
This is none of your business!

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:03.840
Yes, it is!

00:07:04.210 --> 00:07:06.050
This is a dangerous mission.

00:07:06.420 --> 00:07:09.760
If even one person
doesn't follow orders, we could fail!

00:07:09.840 --> 00:07:13.600
You haven't seen the power of
my String Puppet, so you're saying that!

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:14.890
I'll show you right now!

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:15.930
<i>Wait!</i>

00:07:16.560 --> 00:07:18.100
<i>Hold up, would you?</i>

00:07:18.180 --> 00:07:21.770
<i>I'll talk to Gai,</i>
<i>but you need to follow Milo's orders.</i>

00:07:21.850 --> 00:07:25.320
You can protect us even from afar, right?
You're the man.

00:07:26.230 --> 00:07:28.150
Well, I guess so.

00:07:29.820 --> 00:07:31.030
POLICE

00:07:34.620 --> 00:07:35.780
Amazing!

00:07:37.990 --> 00:07:39.540
We demand an explanation!

00:07:39.620 --> 00:07:41.000
Get the Mayor out here!

00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:43.580
You want us to attack?

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:46.000
That's unconstitutional, Kuroiwa.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:49.010
We've already been attacked
by the Revisions.

00:07:49.260 --> 00:07:52.010
Does the constitution even exist
at this point?

00:07:54.090 --> 00:07:57.390
I understand,
but as a nation governed by laws--

00:07:57.470 --> 00:07:58.930
Don't you want to survive?

00:07:59.180 --> 00:08:00.520
I do, but...

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:03.900
The organization
that woman called Milo is a part of,

00:08:04.100 --> 00:08:07.690
the group called AHRV,
can't we meet with them?

00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:10.280
If we can at least find out
when they plan to send us back--

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:12.360
Will the people survive that long?

00:08:12.450 --> 00:08:15.410
We're a bunch of disaster victims
with no relief coming.

00:08:16.830 --> 00:08:20.370
We, the police, have our hands full
just trying to protect the public.

00:08:20.450 --> 00:08:23.040
We won't be able to defend
against the Revisions.

00:08:23.460 --> 00:08:25.330
Since they're an effective deterrent,

00:08:25.420 --> 00:08:28.420
I'd like to put Daisuke Dojima's
Anti-Revisions Wearable Combat System

00:08:28.500 --> 00:08:29.550
at the forefront.

00:08:30.010 --> 00:08:32.340
The problem is the liberal ideologists.

00:08:32.760 --> 00:08:34.970
Human rights, anti-war, and love.

00:08:35.550 --> 00:08:38.350
Those things can only be upheld
in times of peace.

00:08:40.310 --> 00:08:44.100
I'd like to silence them
and solidify our core defense.

00:08:44.190 --> 00:08:50.280
-Well, I'm a liberal...
-Down with the Mayor's dictatorship!

00:08:50.900 --> 00:08:53.150
Hey, does this mean

00:08:54.200 --> 00:08:56.490
we're in the middle of a war?

00:08:56.570 --> 00:08:58.160
Well...

00:08:58.240 --> 00:08:59.910
That's...

00:08:59.990 --> 00:09:01.080
It will be okay.

00:09:01.160 --> 00:09:04.580
They said AHRV is working
to transport us back to our time.

00:09:04.660 --> 00:09:06.960
We just need to protect the city
until then.

00:09:07.040 --> 00:09:09.250
Yes, think of it as a disaster drill.

00:09:09.670 --> 00:09:12.210
And today is more like an adventure.

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:13.720
Like a treasure hunt.

00:09:14.220 --> 00:09:17.640
-We'll be all right. Don't worry.
-Okay.

00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:27.440
I've arrived at the designated location.
I don't see anything abnormal.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:31.400
<i>Roger that. Have you linked</i>
<i>to the enemy detection sensor?</i>

00:09:31.480 --> 00:09:32.320
Yes.

00:09:32.400 --> 00:09:35.240
The String Puppet moves like my own body
while I'm wearing the neurosuit.

00:09:35.320 --> 00:09:36.450
It's incredible.

00:09:36.530 --> 00:09:39.990
<i>I bet it is.</i>
<i>They were made for you, guys.</i>

00:09:40.080 --> 00:09:44.540
You mean the people of the future
prepared this, assuming we would use them?

00:09:44.620 --> 00:09:46.710
<i>-That's right.</i>
<i>-Hold on a second.</i>

00:09:46.790 --> 00:09:50.630
Why is that only we can use
the String Puppets?

00:09:50.710 --> 00:09:52.960
<i>Because that's how they were designed.</i>

00:09:53.050 --> 00:09:55.800
But that means they knew that Shibuya

00:09:55.880 --> 00:09:58.340
would be transported to the future
along with us.

00:09:58.430 --> 00:09:59.470
-What?
-What?

00:09:59.550 --> 00:10:00.390
Why?

00:10:00.470 --> 00:10:02.720
<i>They predicted it</i>
<i>from our activity records.</i>

00:10:03.010 --> 00:10:03.890
What?

00:10:04.060 --> 00:10:05.730
What's an activity record?

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:08.100
<i>I don't know if you'd understand</i>
<i>even if I explained.</i>

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:09.770
Let us decide that.

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:14.860
<i>All right.</i><i>Then I will tell you</i>
<i>as much as I am allowed.</i>

00:10:15.530 --> 00:10:19.530
<i>But before that, let me tell you,</i>
<i>I have the ability to jump through time.</i>

00:10:19.610 --> 00:10:21.280
-What?
-What?

00:10:21.370 --> 00:10:23.740
What does that mean?
Like a psychic power?

00:10:23.830 --> 00:10:27.710
<i>If you can do that,</i>
<i>hurry up and return us to our time.</i>

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:30.420
My power doesn't work that way.

00:10:30.830 --> 00:10:34.500
<i>It's not effective for a group.</i>
<i>Nor can I jump anywhere or anytime.</i>

00:10:35.130 --> 00:10:38.510
<i>There are other AHRV agents</i>
<i>with this power besides me.</i>

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:40.720
<i>They use it to predict the future.</i>

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:43.640
<i>-Does that mean they look at the future?</i>
-<i>It's the opposite.</i>

00:10:43.720 --> 00:10:45.350
The agents leap to the past.

00:10:45.430 --> 00:10:48.560
They go there
to leave useful information in that time.

00:10:48.640 --> 00:10:51.150
AHRV then retrieves
and analyzes that information

00:10:51.230 --> 00:10:53.060
in order to predict the future.

00:10:53.770 --> 00:10:55.070
They go to the past?

00:10:55.230 --> 00:10:57.740
Does that mean they change the future
as they see fit?

00:10:57.820 --> 00:10:58.990
<i>There's no need to worry.</i>

00:10:59.070 --> 00:11:02.870
<i>We use the utmost caution not to change</i>
<i>any important historical events.</i>

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:05.580
<i>-That's not the problem--</i>
-Listen.

00:11:06.160 --> 00:11:09.210
By adjusting the past
and relying on our data,

00:11:09.750 --> 00:11:12.790
we succeeded in predicting a future
where humanity does not perish.

00:11:12.920 --> 00:11:14.670
<i>A future where humanity doesn't perish?</i>

00:11:15.250 --> 00:11:18.510
<i>That's right.</i>
<i>There was a chance humanity would perish.</i>

00:11:18.720 --> 00:11:22.050
<i>To prevent this from happening,</i>
<i>we predicted Shibuya's forced time leap</i>

00:11:22.140 --> 00:11:24.350
<i>and learned that your existence</i>
<i>is vital to the mission.</i>

00:11:24.470 --> 00:11:26.010
Our existence?

00:11:26.390 --> 00:11:27.680
<i>Why us?</i>

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:31.390
<i>Does that have to do with</i>
<i>why you saved Daisuke in the past?</i>

00:11:31.480 --> 00:11:32.650
<i>That I don't know.</i>

00:11:32.900 --> 00:11:37.030
<i>We are simply taught to predict the future</i>
<i>for the good of humanity.</i>

00:11:37.570 --> 00:11:41.360
<i>The Milo we met in the past</i>
<i>during the kidnapping...</i>

00:11:41.950 --> 00:11:42.780
<i>Milo.</i>

00:11:44.990 --> 00:11:48.370
<i>You had been shot by a gun or something.</i>

00:11:49.330 --> 00:11:52.870
That's right!
If my memory serves, you should be dead.

00:11:53.540 --> 00:11:55.210
Gai, what are you saying?

00:11:55.670 --> 00:11:59.420
I'm saying this Milo may be
a different person from the Milo we met.

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:02.130
But she's the same Milo as back then.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:04.800
<i>She's not just a look-alike.</i>

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:06.050
She's not the same.

00:12:06.510 --> 00:12:09.020
The Milo I knew was kinder.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.230
<i>I don't really remember.</i>

00:12:11.310 --> 00:12:12.520
Keisaku!

00:12:12.600 --> 00:12:15.150
We were in elementary school, you know.

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:17.730
It would be weird
if I remembered everything.

00:12:17.820 --> 00:12:19.280
This is just a theory.

00:12:19.610 --> 00:12:22.610
But perhaps the future me
has leaped to that time.

00:12:23.320 --> 00:12:24.660
<i>Why do you think that?</i>

00:12:24.740 --> 00:12:29.160
One thing I can say is
your past is not set in stone.

00:12:30.500 --> 00:12:32.830
Then I wish you'd change my luck.

00:12:32.910 --> 00:12:35.330
I'm always unlucky at critical moments.

00:12:35.420 --> 00:12:36.540
Who cares about that?

00:12:36.630 --> 00:12:38.500
<i>I believe the Milo from that time.</i>

00:12:38.960 --> 00:12:41.710
That's because
I'm protecting everyone now.

00:12:42.970 --> 00:12:43.800
Izumi reporting.

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:46.300
<i>We've arrived at our destination.</i>
<i>Awaiting instructions.</i>

00:12:46.510 --> 00:12:47.430
<i>Roger.</i>

00:12:47.510 --> 00:12:51.310
<i>The remaining two String Puppets</i>
<i>are at the second floor of that building.</i>

00:12:51.390 --> 00:12:53.810
<i>Have the pilots board after finding them.</i>

00:12:53.890 --> 00:12:55.020
<i>Understood.</i>

00:12:55.100 --> 00:12:58.980
Did you hear that, everyone?
Decide now who'll be piloting them.

00:13:01.650 --> 00:13:04.820
Doubt everything.

00:13:05.490 --> 00:13:08.950
Do you understand? Don't forget, Gai.

00:13:15.540 --> 00:13:17.290
Will you be okay alone?

00:13:20.500 --> 00:13:22.210
Oh, a gun.

00:13:22.300 --> 00:13:25.260
I may not look it,
but I am a cop after all.

00:13:26.260 --> 00:13:29.390
Eat your lunch
while I go and check it out.

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:34.600
<i>Single Civilian detected</i>
<i>three kilometers south-southeast.</i>

00:13:35.770 --> 00:13:37.060
It's a bit far.

00:13:38.100 --> 00:13:39.360
Okay!

00:13:42.780 --> 00:13:44.780
Doubt everything.

00:13:45.990 --> 00:13:48.610
Do you understand? Don't forget, Gai.

00:13:51.030 --> 00:13:52.620
Broiled saury.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:55.330
This one is miso mackerel

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:57.540
and sausages?

00:13:58.710 --> 00:14:00.340
And fried rice.

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:02.880
Hey, which one do you want, Gai?

00:14:03.130 --> 00:14:06.340
You know what, I think Milo
is still hiding something.

00:14:06.880 --> 00:14:09.430
She said she can only tell us
what she's allowed to.

00:14:09.510 --> 00:14:12.720
No, I was remembering Milo from the past.

00:14:13.510 --> 00:14:16.230
She told us to doubt everything.

00:14:16.310 --> 00:14:17.390
What?

00:14:17.850 --> 00:14:18.980
You don't remember?

00:14:19.100 --> 00:14:20.810
You've got that flipped, Gai.

00:14:20.900 --> 00:14:21.810
What?

00:14:21.940 --> 00:14:25.990
That's the one thing I remember.
Milo told us to accept everything.

00:14:26.400 --> 00:14:27.860
Accept everything.

00:14:29.410 --> 00:14:30.700
That's what she said.

00:14:30.910 --> 00:14:34.910
So I thought it was a prediction that
we should just accept what happened.

00:14:35.160 --> 00:14:36.580
What? Am I wrong?

00:14:37.910 --> 00:14:39.540
My memory is vague.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:42.790
I could be wrong, but I think she said,

00:14:42.880 --> 00:14:45.420
"Ultimately,
you must decide for yourself."

00:14:45.670 --> 00:14:47.800
It was like she was encouraging me.

00:14:48.130 --> 00:14:51.090
-What about you, Lu?
-I don't remember most of it.

00:14:51.180 --> 00:14:52.300
I see.

00:14:52.510 --> 00:14:54.510
It was a long time ago, after all.

00:14:54.680 --> 00:14:56.850
We keep forgetting more and more.

00:14:57.100 --> 00:14:58.140
You're right.

00:14:58.600 --> 00:15:02.480
And we've avoided talking about
what happened as much as we could.

00:15:02.810 --> 00:15:06.070
I only remember it
when Daisuke says something.

00:15:07.240 --> 00:15:11.240
Besides, why was Daisuke kidnapped
in the first place?

00:15:11.820 --> 00:15:13.830
Why did Milo help us?

00:15:14.280 --> 00:15:16.830
We never figured out the truth
behind that.

00:15:16.910 --> 00:15:17.950
You know what?

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:20.790
Maybe Milo just said something ordinary.

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:21.750
What?

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:25.750
It was only Daisuke who made a big deal
and said it was destiny and stuff.

00:15:30.300 --> 00:15:31.300
This must be it.

00:15:39.680 --> 00:15:41.020
Has it ceased functioning?

00:15:41.600 --> 00:15:44.560
No, there was a signal. It must be asleep.

00:15:44.980 --> 00:15:46.270
It's near the others.

00:15:46.690 --> 00:15:47.900
What if it's a trap?

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:50.110
Daisuke, you're--

00:15:50.190 --> 00:15:52.160
I found them! Both of them!

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:54.280
They look the same as Daisuke's.

00:15:56.410 --> 00:15:58.160
<i>What's happening Daisuke? Respond!</i>

00:15:58.240 --> 00:16:00.120
-I'm in combat.
<i>-What? Where?</i>

00:16:00.200 --> 00:16:01.290
With the enemy!

00:16:01.370 --> 00:16:02.790
You abandoned your position?

00:16:02.870 --> 00:16:06.500
I'm the only one who can defeat it!
Isn't that right?

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:12.130
Did you see that?
It's easy with this thing!

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:13.720
Your mission is to provide cover.

00:16:14.180 --> 00:16:17.140
<i>-You fell for the enemy's diversion!</i>
-Diversion?

00:16:18.260 --> 00:16:19.100
Crap!

00:16:25.150 --> 00:16:28.320
Daisuke, launch covering fire
at the coordinates I just sent you.

00:16:30.070 --> 00:16:31.690
<i>Target coordinate data acquired.</i>

00:16:31.780 --> 00:16:33.990
<i>Strike possible with high-angle fire.</i>

00:16:34.070 --> 00:16:35.820
There's not much I can do with that.

00:16:35.910 --> 00:16:37.620
<i>Hey, Daisuke! Can you hear me?</i>

00:16:37.700 --> 00:16:39.830
Izumi! How is the String Puppet retrieval?

00:16:39.910 --> 00:16:42.790
<i>A Civilian has appeared.</i>
<i>I'll be a decoy and distract it.</i>

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:44.460
Hurry with the retrieval!

00:16:46.960 --> 00:16:47.960
There's one here too!

00:16:48.040 --> 00:16:50.300
Everyone, into the building!
I'll take care of it!

00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:53.340
I may not look it, but I'm a cop!

00:16:53.760 --> 00:16:57.390
<i>This is Kuroiwa from Shibuya.</i>
<i>Respond, Officer Izumi!</i>

00:16:57.470 --> 00:16:59.760
-Yes, sir!
-<i>We've got an emergency!</i>

00:17:00.470 --> 00:17:01.680
<i>A monster has appeared!</i>

00:17:01.770 --> 00:17:03.730
<i>Near the border at highway 246!</i>

00:17:04.140 --> 00:17:05.560
What? There too?

00:17:13.610 --> 00:17:16.990
Kuroiwa, we're not even making a dent!

00:17:17.070 --> 00:17:20.030
I told you!
Our hands are full with public safety!

00:17:20.120 --> 00:17:23.000
-What about that weapon?
<i>-</i>It's still in the Sangenjaya area.

00:17:23.450 --> 00:17:25.580
Get the water cannon
and the rubber bullets!

00:17:25.710 --> 00:17:28.000
I don't know if it'll have any effect,
but the tear gas too!

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:28.960
Yes, sir!

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:32.300
Daisuke!

00:17:32.380 --> 00:17:33.460
Milo!

00:17:36.050 --> 00:17:37.510
Daisuke, do it!

00:17:37.590 --> 00:17:38.590
All right!

00:17:53.690 --> 00:17:55.740
I'm sorry for leaving my post.

00:17:55.820 --> 00:17:57.820
-The others are in danger.
-What?

00:17:57.910 --> 00:18:00.660
They may be able to fight it off
with the String Puppets.

00:18:06.120 --> 00:18:07.960
I'll die in the line of duty.

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:21.470
Activation confirmed.
Who are the pilots?

00:18:22.560 --> 00:18:24.020
Lu and I are piloting.

00:18:24.470 --> 00:18:25.730
Can you both handle them?

00:18:25.810 --> 00:18:27.140
<i>-Well...</i>
<i>-We'll try!</i>

00:18:27.230 --> 00:18:29.810
It might be too much
for rookies to handle.

00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:31.560
I'm on my way to help you out!

00:18:38.490 --> 00:18:40.030
Will those two be okay?

00:18:42.450 --> 00:18:44.080
I've arrived!

00:18:53.340 --> 00:18:55.250
All right, I'll finish them off!

00:18:55.670 --> 00:18:57.760
Don't move. Stay out of the line of fire.

00:19:00.510 --> 00:19:01.970
Adjust to the right, 2.4 degrees.

00:19:02.050 --> 00:19:04.350
Got it. Right, 2.4 degrees.

00:19:08.520 --> 00:19:09.940
-Gai!
-Right!

00:19:16.110 --> 00:19:17.030
Yes!

00:19:17.530 --> 00:19:18.530
These guys...

00:19:19.400 --> 00:19:21.660
They can already pilot them this well?

00:19:22.990 --> 00:19:26.490
-Izumi, what's the situation in Shibuya?
-The Chief just told me.

00:19:26.740 --> 00:19:28.540
Several policemen are dead

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:31.330
and about 15 were taken.

00:19:32.920 --> 00:19:36.210
<i>What? Is that true? The Revisions?</i>

00:19:36.590 --> 00:19:40.130
<i>Yes, they want to meet the person</i>
<i>in charge of this area.</i>

00:19:40.630 --> 00:19:43.680
I don't want to. That's the enemy, right?

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:46.310
-Well, it was a young woman.
-What?

00:19:46.390 --> 00:19:49.810
<i>Her outfit seems like a joke.</i>
<i>It's hard to say if we should trust her.</i>

00:21:23.940 --> 00:21:26.910
A remote communication body?

00:21:27.360 --> 00:21:28.370
That's right.

00:21:28.450 --> 00:21:32.830
I chose a form you would find easier
to empathize with.

00:21:33.330 --> 00:21:35.460
It makes it easier to negotiate.

00:21:35.540 --> 00:21:38.330
You should take it as a sign
of our good faith.

00:21:44.920 --> 00:21:46.260
I see.

00:21:46.340 --> 00:21:51.510
So you're saying you, the Revisions,
are the victims of the pandemic we caused?

00:21:51.720 --> 00:21:52.720
That's right.

00:21:52.890 --> 00:21:56.980
You're saying that the disease
that wiped out humanity is our fault?

00:21:57.060 --> 00:21:59.940
No, we're not asking you
to take the blame.

00:22:00.020 --> 00:22:02.980
The RV virus just happened to appear
during your time.

00:22:03.070 --> 00:22:04.150
That's all.

00:22:05.030 --> 00:22:08.200
We have spent a long time
preparing for this plan.

00:22:09.070 --> 00:22:13.450
However, in order to execute it,
your cooperation is necessary.

00:22:13.580 --> 00:22:14.410
What?

00:22:14.500 --> 00:22:18.080
By changing the past,
we change the present. A revision.

00:22:18.170 --> 00:22:19.040
What?

00:22:19.120 --> 00:22:23.250
We will send those on this list
back to their original time first.

00:22:23.550 --> 00:22:26.970
We will not guarantee the safety
of those not on the list.

00:22:32.560 --> 00:22:36.560
They're telling us to sacrifice some
in order to save others.

00:22:42.610 --> 00:22:47.440
This is what I'd definitely call
a high-level government decision.

00:22:49.860 --> 00:22:52.070
Subtitle translation by Emily Noguchi
